    "message": "feat(admin): persist analytics filters + page across refresh, add Clear filters\n\nSite persistence previously remembered only the active view, auto-refresh and\nweb-search period. An F5 on the Analytics page lost every filter. Now:\n\n- persistDashboardState saves the analytics filters (provider, model, key,\n  search, status, endpoint, window, page size) plus the page offset.\n- load() restores them so a refresh continues the same query.\n- New \"Clear filters\" button resets every filter to its default and reloads\n  the view in place.\n\nTwo robustness fixes found while verifying in a real browser:\n\n1. restoreDashboardState() returned an empty object when called at the very\n   start of load(), because the browser was still settling localStorage during\n   the initial synchronous script execution. Reading it after the first await\n   (loadOnboarding) makes the read reliable — reproduced in both jsdom and a\n   live browser before the fix.\n2. Navigation during the initial load persisted half-restored state (empty\n   filters) over the saved state, clobbering it. A state.loading guard now\n   blocks persistDashboardState() during load(), cleared in a finally so an\n   error can never leave persistence disabled.\n\nVerified in a real browser on a throwaway server (port 8163, fake home): set\nfilters -> Apply -> reload -> all filters + view restore; Clear filters resets\nevery input, reloads, and persists the cleared state. 100 admin/docs-label\ntests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
